{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Every method above except scPRINT runs the full accuracy/speed/memory matrix of \u167 ?3.1\u8211-\u167 ?3.2 on all six datasets, so no method is compared on only a subset. Two are deliberately outside that matrix, each for a stated reason: - {\b scPRINT} is a zero-shot foundation model with a {\i fixed} Cell-Ontology label vocabulary; it cannot emit labels outside that set and skips symbol-keyed datasets, so it is not a drop-in reference classifier. We report it separately as the \u8220"just use a foundation model\u8221" reference point (\u167 ?3.7, and externally in \u167 ?3.8). - {\b scPred} is excluded outright: unmaintained; it requires harmony\u8217's removed {\f1 HarmonyMatrix} API and older harmony versions do not compile on the current toolchain.\par}
